==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
This stage doesn't play out too differently during the start but when the base is hit, Zapy is here to greet you! Zapy is weaker in stats compared to [[Capy]] but has a faster attack rate and movement speed. Thankfully she keeps her Single Target and cannot burrow, meaning that plenty of meatshields will suffice. These Shibalien Elites are quite weak once you have collected enough [[Treasure]]s and even without them, strong attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] are enough to take care of them.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Assuming that you have all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]] from all 3 chapters, this stage should be incredibly easy. The Shibalien Elites are pathetic, as are the Zoges. The only thing you might need to worry about is the Zrocos, which can burrow under your limited units and shred your base, but just leave a spot or 2 open for an emergency [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] and you should be good.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The key to this stage is meatshielding while Ubers with decent range (and preferably pierce) chip the Mega Baa Baas, which are the main threat of the stage. While they are easily countered by heavy meatshielding, the other threats with them can quickly eliminate your stacks. Bring a [[Barrier Breaker]] such as [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]] to dispose of the UltraBaaBaas and a Crowd Controller, especially [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]], to help with the GreGories. Also, [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] can take care of the Zombie peons, though falters against the larger threats unless heavily invested in.

